# V-90 Reflections

V-90 Reflections has the original unit's early-reflection programs. Instead of a smooth reverb tail, they produce a pattern of distinct reflections: for ambience, room sound, and the gated and reverse effects of the 1980s.

![V-90 Reflections](../images/reflections.png)

| Memory | Program | Character |
|---|---|---|
| 5 | Early Ref. 1 | Early reflections of a room, hall or plate. |
| 6 | Early Ref. 2 | A second early-reflection program with the same controls and a different sound. |
| 16 | Gate Reverb | A dense burst of reflections that stops abruptly, like a gated reverb. |
| 17 | Reverse Gate | Reflections that build up instead of dying away, like a reversed reverb. |

All four programs have the same parameters, with their own factory settings.

## Parameters

The defaults shown are Early Ref. 1's.

{{table reflections 5}}

### Reflection Types

| TYPE | Pattern |
|---|---|
| HALL | Reflections spaced as in a concert hall. |
| RANDOM | Irregularly spaced reflections. |
| REVERSE | Reflections that grow louder, for a reverse effect. |
| PLATE | Dense reflections, like a plate reverb. |

### Factory Settings

| Program | TYPE | ROOM SIZE | LIVENESS | DELAY | LPF | BALANCE |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Early Ref. 1 | HALL | 2.0 | 5 | 10.0 ms | THRU | 100 % |
| Early Ref. 2 | HALL | 2.0 | 5 | 10.0 ms | THRU | 100 % |
| Gate Reverb | RANDOM | 2.0 | 5 | 20.0 ms | 6.3 kHz | 100 % |
| Reverse Gate | REVERSE | 3.3 | 5 | 25.0 ms | THRU | 100 % |

## AAX DSP

V-90 Reflections runs as AAX Native only.
